2. Does the autoregressive failure shrink with T or with persistence?
==========================================================================

   rho           T=125           T=250           T=500
--------------------------------------------------------
   0.0     1.341 ±0.032     1.275 ±0.028     1.267 ±0.039
   0.5     1.492 ±0.036     1.405 ±0.031     1.365 ±0.043
  0.85     1.918 ±0.047     1.735 ±0.043     1.627 ±0.054
  0.95     2.370 ±0.064     2.067 ±0.063     1.819 ±0.057

Read the rho = 0.85 row: that is the first-order autocorrelation of log realized
variance, so it is where the SPY design sits. R does not approach one as T grows -- a
fourfold increase in the window moves it from 1.92 to 1.53 -- so this is an O(1) failure
of Lemma 1, not a finite-sample effect that a longer window would cure.

